---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import GuideList from "../../components/GuideList.astro";
import Simple from "../../layouts/Simple.astro";
import { visitIdsForArticle } from "../../data/catalog";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles", ({ data }) => data.section === "pricing")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
---
<Simple
  title="Analytics Pricing Guides"
  description="Analytics pricing for DataFast, PostHog, Mixpanel, and Amplitude. Compare free allowances, the first paid step, and fixed monthly plans before you add a card."
  kicker="Pricing"
  lede="Read the first paid step at your volume before you compare logos. Some products publish a monthly tier. Others stay free inside an allowance, then bill usage."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Pricing" }]}
>
  <p>DataFast, the analytics product at datafa.st, publishes monthly event tiers on its homepage. Starter is from $9 a month and Growth is from $19 a month. Both figures are published starting prices for 10,000 monthly events. The <a href="/pricing/datafast/">DataFast pricing</a> guide is that ladder, as of 26 November 2026. The <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a> covers what the product is, and which other companies share the name.</p>
  <p>PostHog, Mixpanel, and Amplitude publish a free event allowance and then charge for volume. The useful question is what the first paid step costs at your volume. Plausible and Fathom price marketing analytics by pageviews, and standard GA4 is free. Those figures are also on the <a href="/alternatives/">alternatives hub</a> and the <a href="/compare/">compare hub</a>.</p>
  <p>Where a vendor publishes a $0 starting price and then a calculator or a quote, the guide says so. Confirm the current rate before you buy.</p>
  <section slot="wide" class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="article-wide">
      <h2>Analytics pricing</h2>
      <GuideList
        items={articles.map((article) => ({
          href: `/${article.id}/`,
          title: article.data.title,
          description: article.data.description,
          visits: visitIdsForArticle(article.id),
        }))}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</Simple>
